// ── D2: the cast arm must also gate the `Discriminant` dest it READS ────────

/// SYNTHETIC MIR — the only fixture here that rustc did not emit. Built by editing the
/// `-Ztrust-dump` capture of
///
///   pub fn disc_dest_merged_cast(e: E, c: bool, b: u64, arr: &[u8;4]) -> u8 {
///       let d: u64 = if c { e as u64 } else { b }; arr[d as usize] }
///
/// so that the MERGED local is the `Discriminant` destination `_6` (bb1
/// `_6 = Discriminant(e)`, bb2 `_6 = b as i64`) and the cast destination `_5` keeps its
/// single def in the join block (bb3 `_5 = move _6 as u64; arr[_5]`). rustc-BUILT MIR
/// gives every `Rvalue::Discriminant` a fresh single-def temp, so no rustc source was
/// found that reaches this shape; the gate is fail-closed defence for the other MIR
/// producers (the extractor, trust-ir, hand-written IR) and is measured here.
///
/// EDITING THE BODY MEANS EDITING THE `preconditions` TOO. The capture carried
/// `_6 ∈ {0, 1}` as a whole-function precondition — `trust_mir_extract`'s
/// `enum_discriminant_range_preconditions`, keyed on the `Discriminant` DESTINATION.
/// That pass gates on `write_counts.get(&d) == Some(1)`, so for the edited body (`_6`
/// written twice) it emits nothing, and a capture of this shape could not carry the
/// clause. Leaving it in made the fixture assert a premise no extraction of its own
/// body can produce — a SECOND, independent vacuity channel sitting in front of the
/// producer this row is about. It is removed, and the clause bounding `b` is kept.
///
/// MEASURED (in-process ay, this crate), on the corrected fixture: the
/// `IndexOutOfBounds` row is `Failed` with witness `d = 4` on a `[u8; 4]`, and it is
/// `Proved` under EITHER of the two gates deleted on its own — the cast arm's
/// `dest.local` conjunct, or the `Discriminant`-dest conjunct that guards
/// `tag_var_sets.push(dest)`. The Rust source above panics 8/32
/// (b in 0..8 x c in {false,true} x e in {A, B}).
#[test]
fn merged_disc_dest_cast_index_still_refutes() {
    assert_refutes(MIR_DISC_DEST_MERGED_CAST, is_bounds, 0, "disc_dest_merged_cast");
}

