// ── THE PRICE OF THE GATE, MEASURED ─────────────────────────────────────────

/// The corrected count refuses to emit a producer's fact when its keyed local is a
/// PARAMETER reassigned while its ENTRY VALUE IS STILL LIVE — and there is no other
/// spelling available: the bare name is the only symbol these producers render, and it
/// is two-valued. So the SAFE row of the same function (the edge that DID run the
/// reassignment) loses its proof too. That is a genuine decline, not an avoidable one:
/// recovering it needs the fact emitted under the DEF-SITE VERSIONED spelling, which
/// is a different mechanism.
///
/// EACH OF THE FOUR REASSIGNS THE PARAMETER UNDER `if c` AND READS IT AFTER THE JOIN,
/// so the incoming argument is observable on the other edge — that is what makes the
/// decline genuine, and it is the only shape that declines. A parameter whose store
/// dominates every mention of it keeps all of its facts:
/// `tests/entry_def_structural.rs` measures seven such programs, four of which an
/// earlier unconditional version of this budget lost (two to a FALSE REFUTATION of a
/// correct program).
///
/// The workaround for the four below is in the four `fresh_local_*` controls above:
/// bind the bounded value to a NEW local and every one of them proves and
/// kernel-certifies again.
///
/// This test FAILS if a row is ever recovered — that is progress, and the row belongs
/// in `assert_refutes(.., want_proved + 1, ..)` with this doc updated.
///
/// `p13c_castbound` HAS BEEN RECOVERED and left this list: see
/// `param_cast_upper_bound_still_refutes`, which now pins one proved row and one
/// refuted one. The three below still pay.
#[test]
fn the_parameter_budget_costs_these_safe_rows() {
    for (name, mir, want) in [
        ("p05_modulo", MIR_P05_MODULO, is_bounds as fn(&VcKind) -> bool),
        ("p09_bitmask", MIR_P09_BITMASK, is_bounds),
        ("p07b_divlt", MIR_P07B_DIVLT, is_bounds),
    ] {
        let rows = rows_of(mir, want);
        assert_eq!(rows.len(), 2, "{name}: the fixture has one safe and one vacuous row");
        assert!(
            rows.iter().all(|(r, _)| !is_proved(r)),
            "{name}: the SAFE row is back — promote it (see this test's doc); got {rows:?}"
        );
    }
}
